==Spanish==

===Punctuation mark===
{{head|es|punctuation mark|head=[[¿]] [[?]]}}

# Used in [[¿ ?]]
# {{lb|es|nonstandard}} Marks a preceding passage as a [[question]], without the starting ¿, as in English and other languages
#: {{uxi|es|Cómo estás'''?'''|How are you'''?'''}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|es|%C2%BF %3F|¿ ?}}
* {{l|es|%C2%A1 %21|¡ !}}

====Usage notes====
* As [[SMS]] messaging and other forms of electronic communication have become more common, some Spanish-speakers use only ? for questions and ! for exclamations, leaving out the initial typographical mark. This is considered non-standard usage.